## Findings
F1.1 ac=scope at=src/superclaude/agents/eval-docs-loader.md:29 anchor="AUG phrase (full form, verbatim): \"Codebase search: call `mcp__litellm__augment_code-augment_code_search` (`repo_owner`/`repo_name` from `git remote get-url origin`, `branch` = the repository's default branch; it sees pushed code only); if that tool is not available, call `mcp__auggie__codebase-retrieval`. For uncommitted or unpushed changes use codegraph or Grep.\"" chk=n,n,n,y family=aug-phrase-verbatim fix=Restore the start-snapshot wording in both files and, if the line-based guard flags it, join the phrase onto one line (as src/superclaude/skills/sc-auggie-review-protocol/SKILL.md:226, src/superclaude/agents/rf-team-lead.md:149 and src/superclaude/skills/sc-validate-roadmap-protocol/SKILL.md:262 already do) instead of reordering it; keep finding-verify.md's task-specific "PR head branch; it sees pushed commits only" wording. covers="AUG phrase (full form, verbatim)": To make the per-line guard pass, the implementer rewrote two already-compliant full-form AUG phrases into a different word order: "Codebase search (`repo_owner`/... pushed code only):\ncall `mcp__litellm__augment_code-augment_code_search`; if that tool is not available, call ..." at src/superclaude/agents/eval-docs-loader.md:29-32 and src/superclaude/skills/sc-pr-submit-protocol/refs/finding-verify.md:33-36. The constraint requires the full form verbatim ("Codebase search: call AUG (repo_owner...); if that tool is not available, ..."); the start snapshot had it verbatim (wrapped). These were guard false positives, not missed call sites, and a one-line join would have satisfied the guard without breaking the phrase.

F1.2 ac=scope at=tests/skills/test_mcp_proxy_names.py:23 anchor=tests/skills/test_mcp_proxy_names.py:3 chk=n,n,n,n family=guard-coverage fix=Optionally extend the Tavily check to YAML block-list allow-lists (track that a `tools:`/`allowed-tools:` key with an empty value opens a block, and require each `- mcp__tavily__tavily_<x>` item to be preceded by a `- mcp__litellm__Tavily-tavily_<x>` item in the same block), or narrow the module docstring to the rules actually enforced. : `_TOOLS_LINE` only matches single-line allow-lists, so the Tavily rule never inspects the YAML block-list `tools:` form used by 14 agents (for example src/superclaude/agents/rf-analyst.md:6-16, src/superclaude/agents/deep-research.md:5-13, src/superclaude/agents/rf-qa.md:6-16). Those files are currently correct (proxy item immediately before each direct item), but deleting a proxy item there would not fail the guard. The docstring at :3-4 ("Every installed primitive that names a direct MCP tool must also name its `mcp__litellm__` proxy twin") is broader than what is enforced (no Context7 check, no block-list Tavily check). The brief's own wording is per-line ("every tools:/allowed-tools: line"), so this is a coverage gap rather than an AC breach; advisory.

F1.3 ac=scope at=.dev/tasks/to-do/TASK-WF-refactorAllMcpTo-20261108-150855/artifacts/t15-guard.log:1 anchor=".dev/tasks/ is always staged (`git add .dev/tasks`)" chk=n,n,n,n family=staging fix=Run `git add .dev/tasks` (orchestrator step) so t15-guard.log and t15-pytest.log are staged like the T1-T13 artifacts. : At review time `git status` shows artifacts/t15-guard.log and artifacts/t15-pytest.log as untracked (`??`) while earlier task artifacts are staged. Likely the orchestrator's staging step has not run yet, so recorded as advisory only.
